00:14:42.000 --> 00:15:11.000
war. But still, the Daily Chronicle, we must not fight the Germans. It says, the great people whose civilization is in many ways the most akin in Europe to our own. The idea of a ruinous conflict between us seems more unqualifiedly distasteful now than it has perhaps for a generation. So that's again picking up on the idea that actually Anglo-German relations have been improving. Exactly. It's so interesting and so counterintuitive, given everything that we believe about the road to the First World War. The cabinet meets again. Still, they can't decide.
但《每日纪事报》仍然说：“我们绝不能与德国人作战。”它说：“这个伟大的民族，其文明在许多方面是欧洲与我们最相似的。在我们之间发生毁灭性冲突的想法，现在比一代人以来任何时候都更令人反感。”所以这又回到了 Anglo-German 关系实际上一直在改善的想法。完全正确。这非常有趣，而且非常违反直觉，考虑到我们关于第一次世界大战之路所相信的一切。内阁再次开会。他们仍然无法决定。

